1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,357
Ferrari closed the order book on its

2
00:00:02,357 --> 00:00:05,174
first four-door car before it had delivered

3
00:00:05,174 --> 00:00:06,025
a single one.

4
00:00:06,205 --> 00:00:09,571
The Ferrari Purosangue has no anti-roll bars

5
00:00:09,571 --> 00:00:10,106
at all.

6
00:00:10,286 --> 00:00:13,129
And its chief executive asked the world

7
00:00:13,129 --> 00:00:14,733
not to call it an SUV.

8
00:00:14,913 --> 00:00:17,056
These are two of the things you

9
00:00:17,056 --> 00:00:19,960
may not know about the Ferrari Purosangue:

10
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,689
how its suspension works,

11
00:00:21,689 --> 00:00:24,317
and why Ferrari stopped taking orders.

12
00:00:24,497 --> 00:00:26,389
Everything here is sourced.

13
00:00:26,739 --> 00:00:28,479
We read Wikipedia,

14
00:00:28,479 --> 00:00:30,413
Motor1, Robb Report,

15
00:00:30,413 --> 00:00:33,699
Carscoops, autoevolution, Autocar,

16
00:00:33,699 --> 00:00:37,469
Autoblog and a Czech business site that

17
00:00:37,469 --> 00:00:40,079
analysed Ferrari's results.

18
00:00:40,259 --> 00:00:43,481
Ferrari's own performance figures are claims,

19
00:00:43,481 --> 00:00:45,414
and we mark them as claims.

20
00:00:45,594 --> 00:00:47,947
Prices conflict between sources,

21
00:00:47,947 --> 00:00:49,565
and we show every one.

22
00:00:49,745 --> 00:00:53,077
And our own arithmetic is always labelled

23
00:00:53,077 --> 00:00:53,727
as ours.

24
00:00:54,077 --> 00:00:56,134
Motor1's Brian Silvestro,

25
00:00:56,134 --> 00:01:00,414
reviewing the Purosangue in July twenty twenty-four,

26
00:01:00,414 --> 00:01:03,295
describes its suspension in detail.

27
00:01:03,475 --> 00:01:06,856
The dampers are Multimatic's True Active Spool

28
00:01:06,856 --> 00:01:09,796
Valve type, which use electric motors to

29
00:01:09,796 --> 00:01:12,147
control damping and ride height.

30
00:01:12,327 --> 00:01:15,173
The left and right sides work independently,

31
00:01:15,173 --> 00:01:17,242
and the review says there are no

32
00:01:17,242 --> 00:01:17,889
sway bars.

33
00:01:18,239 --> 00:01:20,637
The review says that in soft mode

34
00:01:20,637 --> 00:01:22,744
the car is composed but firm,

35
00:01:22,744 --> 00:01:25,578
and that hard mode stiffens the dampers

36
00:01:25,578 --> 00:01:27,759
and greatly reduces body roll.

37
00:01:27,939 --> 00:01:30,588
Silvestro writes that it handles more like

38
00:01:30,588 --> 00:01:32,606
a sports sedan than a crossover.

39
00:01:32,786 --> 00:01:34,998
We cannot measure that ourselves,

40
00:01:34,998 --> 00:01:37,948
and the review reports no cornering numbers,

41
00:01:37,948 --> 00:01:40,228
so it is one reviewer's judgement.

42
00:01:40,578 --> 00:01:42,551
The same review gives its verdict.

43
00:01:42,731 --> 00:01:45,866
It calls the Purosangue the best SUV-shaped

44
00:01:45,866 --> 00:01:47,835
vehicle he has ever driven,

45
00:01:47,835 --> 00:01:50,022
and says it is not even close.

46
00:01:50,202 --> 00:01:52,836
It names the Cadillac CT five V

47
00:01:52,836 --> 00:01:55,471
Blackwing and the BMW M five CS

48
00:01:55,471 --> 00:01:57,340
as the closest rivals,

49
00:01:57,340 --> 00:02:00,569
and says the Ferrari is more enjoyable

50
00:02:00,569 --> 00:02:01,928
on twisty roads.

51
00:02:02,108 --> 00:02:03,984
The review does not compare it with

52
00:02:03,984 --> 00:02:05,324
the Rolls-Royce Cullinan.

53
00:02:05,675 --> 00:02:08,101
Wikipedia gives the base hardware.

54
00:02:08,281 --> 00:02:12,038
A six point five litre naturally aspirated

55
00:02:12,038 --> 00:02:14,811
V12, called the F one forty IA,

56
00:02:14,811 --> 00:02:18,210
with seven hundred fifteen horsepower,

57
00:02:18,210 --> 00:02:21,161
seven hundred twenty-five metric,

58
00:02:21,161 --> 00:02:23,576
at seventy-seven fifty rpm,

59
00:02:23,576 --> 00:02:28,317
and five hundred twenty-eight pound-feet at sixty-two

60
00:02:28,317 --> 00:02:28,854
fifty.

61
00:02:29,034 --> 00:02:31,566
It drives all four wheels through an

62
00:02:31,566 --> 00:02:33,817
eight-speed dual-clutch gearbox,

63
00:02:33,817 --> 00:02:36,279
with a redline of eighty-two fifty.

64
00:02:36,629 --> 00:02:37,962
By our arithmetic,

65
00:02:37,962 --> 00:02:41,444
seven hundred fifteen horsepower from six point

66
00:02:41,444 --> 00:02:44,482
five litres is one hundred ten horsepower

67
00:02:44,482 --> 00:02:46,927
per litre, with no turbochargers.

68
00:02:47,107 --> 00:02:49,557
Ferrari's claims, per Wikipedia:

69
00:02:49,557 --> 00:02:52,544
zero to one hundred kilometres per hour

70
00:02:52,544 --> 00:02:54,764
in three point three seconds,

71
00:02:54,764 --> 00:02:57,215
zero to two hundred in ten point

72
00:02:57,215 --> 00:02:59,359
six, and a top speed of over

73
00:02:59,359 --> 00:03:02,269
three hundred ten kilometres per hour.

74
00:03:02,449 --> 00:03:03,637
By our arithmetic,

75
00:03:03,637 --> 00:03:05,684
the gap from one hundred to two

76
00:03:05,684 --> 00:03:08,126
hundred is seven point three seconds.

77
00:03:08,477 --> 00:03:11,194
Motor1 lists zero to sixty at three

78
00:03:11,194 --> 00:03:12,592
point two seconds,

79
00:03:12,592 --> 00:03:14,688
but labels it as estimated,

80
00:03:14,688 --> 00:03:15,698
not measured.

81
00:03:15,878 --> 00:03:18,015
Its spec sheet gives a top speed

82
00:03:18,015 --> 00:03:20,753
of one hundred ninety-two miles per hour,

83
00:03:20,753 --> 00:03:23,491
which is three hundred nine kilometres an

84
00:03:23,491 --> 00:03:25,027
hour by our arithmetic.

85
00:03:25,207 --> 00:03:28,353
Wikipedia's figure is over three hundred ten.

86
00:03:28,533 --> 00:03:31,284
The numbers are close but not identical,

87
00:03:31,284 --> 00:03:33,692
and all of them come from Ferrari's

88
00:03:33,692 --> 00:03:34,036
side.

89
00:03:34,385 --> 00:03:35,488
The second thing.

90
00:03:35,668 --> 00:03:39,133
Robb Report says Ferrari temporarily closed the

91
00:03:39,133 --> 00:03:42,008
Purosangue's order book about two and a

92
00:03:42,008 --> 00:03:44,072
half months after its debut,

93
00:03:44,072 --> 00:03:47,242
because interest far outpaced what it could

94
00:03:47,242 --> 00:03:47,685
build.

95
00:03:47,865 --> 00:03:50,663
The waiting list was roughly two years.

96
00:03:50,843 --> 00:03:52,325
And Enrico Galliera,

97
00:03:52,325 --> 00:03:54,846
Ferrari's chief marketing officer,

98
00:03:54,846 --> 00:03:57,588
said: We had such an interest without

99
00:03:57,588 --> 00:03:59,515
delivering one single car.

100
00:03:59,865 --> 00:04:02,972
Carscoops adds that on the earnings call

101
00:04:02,972 --> 00:04:05,070
in May twenty twenty-three,

102
00:04:05,070 --> 00:04:08,798
chief executive Benedetto Vigna said Ferrari was

103
00:04:08,798 --> 00:04:10,895
preparing to reopen orders.

104
00:04:11,075 --> 00:04:13,261
He said the company had been caught

105
00:04:13,261 --> 00:04:16,009
by positive surprise by the strong interest.

106
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:19,177
Anyone who ordered then would wait until

107
00:04:19,177 --> 00:04:21,193
at least twenty twenty-six.

108
00:04:21,373 --> 00:04:24,279
Motor1 later reported that order books were

109
00:04:24,279 --> 00:04:25,901
at their highest levels.

110
00:04:26,250 --> 00:04:27,946
There was a promise attached.

111
00:04:28,126 --> 00:04:31,174
Robb Report, Carscoops and Motor1 all say

112
00:04:31,174 --> 00:04:33,777
the Purosangue will make up no more

113
00:04:33,777 --> 00:04:36,752
than twenty percent of Ferrari's output.

114
00:04:36,932 --> 00:04:39,911
Carscoops says Vigna also pledged not to

115
00:04:39,911 --> 00:04:42,146
extend the model's life cycle,

116
00:04:42,146 --> 00:04:43,561
despite the demand.

117
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:46,139
That means the promise is a ceiling

118
00:04:46,139 --> 00:04:48,195
on volume and a limit on time,

119
00:04:48,195 --> 00:04:50,045
both stated by the company.

120
00:04:50,395 --> 00:04:51,847
Put numbers on that cap.

121
00:04:52,027 --> 00:04:55,105
A Czech business site reports that Ferrari

122
00:04:55,105 --> 00:04:57,157
delivered thirteen thousand,

123
00:04:57,157 --> 00:05:00,456
six hundred forty cars in twenty twenty-five.

124
00:05:00,636 --> 00:05:01,902
By our arithmetic,

125
00:05:01,902 --> 00:05:04,646
twenty percent of that is two thousand,

126
00:05:04,646 --> 00:05:06,545
seven hundred twenty-eight.

127
00:05:06,725 --> 00:05:07,886
That is a ceiling,

128
00:05:07,886 --> 00:05:08,659
not a count,

129
00:05:08,659 --> 00:05:10,722
and the article does not say how

130
00:05:10,722 --> 00:05:12,785
many Purosangues were delivered.

131
00:05:13,135 --> 00:05:15,794
An analyst once guessed at the volume.

132
00:05:15,974 --> 00:05:17,920
In August twenty seventeen,

133
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:21,596
Autocar quoted analyst Max Warburton estimating two

134
00:05:21,596 --> 00:05:24,407
thousand to three thousand units a year

135
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:26,713
for the model he called the FUV.

136
00:05:26,893 --> 00:05:28,286
By our arithmetic,

137
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:31,381
that is almost exactly the range implied

138
00:05:31,381 --> 00:05:34,088
by the twenty percent cap on twenty

139
00:05:34,088 --> 00:05:35,868
twenty-five deliveries.

140
00:05:36,048 --> 00:05:38,360
It is an estimate made five years

141
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:40,042
before the car appeared.

142
00:05:40,391 --> 00:05:43,258
Early shipments give a sense of Ferrari's

143
00:05:43,258 --> 00:05:43,677
scale.

144
00:05:43,857 --> 00:05:46,247
Carscoops reports three thousand,

145
00:05:46,247 --> 00:05:49,506
five hundred sixty-seven units shipped in the

146
00:05:49,506 --> 00:05:52,185
first quarter of twenty twenty-three,

147
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:54,213
up nine point seven percent.

148
00:05:54,393 --> 00:05:56,831
If twenty percent of a quarter like

149
00:05:56,831 --> 00:05:58,364
that were Purosangues,

150
00:05:58,364 --> 00:06:00,802
by our arithmetic it would be about

151
00:06:00,802 --> 00:06:02,752
seven hundred fourteen cars.

152
00:06:02,932 --> 00:06:05,152
That is a hypothetical ceiling,

153
00:06:05,152 --> 00:06:07,658
since the car was still ramping up.

154
00:06:08,007 --> 00:06:09,308
Third, the name.

155
00:06:09,488 --> 00:06:13,277
Wikipedia says Purosangue is Italian for the

156
00:06:13,277 --> 00:06:16,550
horse breed, with a link to Purosangue

157
00:06:16,550 --> 00:06:18,962
Orientale, the Arabian type.

158
00:06:19,142 --> 00:06:20,259
In twenty twenty,

159
00:06:20,259 --> 00:06:22,624
Ferrari tried to trademark the name,

160
00:06:22,624 --> 00:06:25,318
but the Purosangue Foundation blocked it.

161
00:06:25,498 --> 00:06:27,647
Ferrari sued, and the case went to

162
00:06:27,647 --> 00:06:29,795
court on the fifth of March twenty

163
00:06:29,795 --> 00:06:30,490
twenty-one.

164
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:32,639
The page does not tell us how

165
00:06:32,639 --> 00:06:33,569
the case ended.

166
00:06:33,749 --> 00:06:35,862
But Ferrari kept the name for the

167
00:06:35,862 --> 00:06:38,486
car, which was revealed on the thirteenth

168
00:06:38,486 --> 00:06:40,471
of September twenty twenty-two.

169
00:06:40,651 --> 00:06:44,231
Wikipedia also says Ferrari does not call

170
00:06:44,231 --> 00:06:45,105
it an SUV,

171
00:06:45,105 --> 00:06:46,065
but an FUV,

172
00:06:46,065 --> 00:06:48,335
