175
00:06:53,226 --> 00:06:55,920
Wikipedia also records an award.

176
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:59,612
The Purosangue won the Compasso d'Oro industrial

177
00:06:59,612 --> 00:07:02,172
design award in twenty twenty-four.

178
00:07:02,352 --> 00:07:04,986
The page gives no jury statement or

179
00:07:04,986 --> 00:07:07,319
reasons, so we do not know what

180
00:07:07,319 --> 00:07:08,749
the judges praised.

181
00:07:08,929 --> 00:07:11,592
The design itself came from the Ferrari

182
00:07:11,592 --> 00:07:14,049
Styling Centre under Flavio Manzoni,

183
00:07:14,049 --> 00:07:15,756
according to the infobox.

184
00:07:16,105 --> 00:07:18,695
The rear doors are unusual.

185
00:07:18,875 --> 00:07:21,910
Wikipedia says they open from the front,

186
00:07:21,910 --> 00:07:23,580
with a fixed B-pillar,

187
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:26,084
to help access to the rear seats.

188
00:07:26,264 --> 00:07:29,055
The infobox calls them coach doors,

189
00:07:29,055 --> 00:07:32,404
while the text calls them front-opening or

190
00:07:32,404 --> 00:07:33,521
suicide-style.

191
00:07:33,701 --> 00:07:36,682
Autoevolution adds that the car has two

192
00:07:36,682 --> 00:07:40,045
